      "title": "Psalm 51 - (Joy Again)",
      "description": "'Psalm 51' (Shame Into Joy) is the 6th installment in the Jubilee Church 'The Psalms of Summer' worship collective\n\nThese worship songs accompany our 'Psalms of Summer' sermon series. Each song is based on one of the books of Psalms. As David wrote songs to express his love for God and at times, his need for rescue and forgiveness, we also express our need for Him in our lives and we rejoice over what He has done for us!!!\n\nLet this song remind us of God's presence in our lives! We sing Hallelujah for His goodness and joy everlasting. Our hearts cannot contain this praise!!!!\n\nLyrics\n\nI am desperate\nI am broken\nFull of regret\nOf grief and heartache\n\nAll I have done\nYou have seen it\nEverything lay\nBare before you\n\nBut this I know to be true\nYou take my heart shattered and bruised\n\nFull of mercy\nBringing healing\nWaves of love and\nSeas of compassion\n\nFountains of grace\nJoy everlasting\nChanging my future\nTurning my mourning to dancing\n\nAnd this will always be true\nThat my spirit has been renewed.\n\nYou have washed all my sins away\nYour mercy comes like a flood each day\nYou’ve created in me a heart that is bursting with praise\nI will sing of Your joy again\n\nUnlock my lips to sing\nMy shame has turned to joy\nMy heart cannot contain\nThe praises of my God",
