      "title": "Psalm 30 (God/Good/Faithful)",
      "description": "'Psalm 30' is part of the 'The Psalms of Summer' worship collective\n\nThese worship songs accompany our 'Psalms of Summer' sermon series. Each song is based on one of the books of Psalms. As David wrote songs to express his love for God and at times, his need for rescue and forgiveness, we also express our need for Him in our lives!\n\nWe pray that these songs help usher you into a deeper connection with God through His Holy Spirit.\n\nLyrics:\n\nWhen all hope was gone\nAnd the lights went out\nAnd I wept all through the night\nI cried out for mercy\n“Oh God can You hear me?”\n\nWhen I felt the weight\nAs it crippled me\nAnd depression took its hold\nI cried out for mercy\n“Oh God can You hear me?”\n\nYou lifted me on high\nBrought me triumph in the night\nAnd turned my wailing into praise\nYour anger passed me by\nBut Your favor is for life\nYour love for me never fails\n\nI know You hear me when I cry\nYour hope will last all through the night\nI know that You are always near\nYou are God You are good\nYou are faithful\n\nWhat can stop my heart\nFrom singing praise\nLike a choir in my soul\nI testify of mercy\nAnd I give You all the glory\n\nYou life me higher and higher\nSo I’ll lift You higher and higher\nWe’ll lift you higher and higher\n\nYou lifted me on high\nBrought me triumph in the night\nAnd turned my wailing into praise\nOh God of grace and mercy\nI give thanks for how You’ve healed me\nOh God of grace and mercy\nI give You all the glory",
